# {{name}}: screens

One section per screen: what it shows, what each control does, and what is
not done. Keep it true; it is what a reader checks the app against.

## Home

Where the app opens.

| Element | Does |
| --- | --- |
| "Hello, <name>." | The stored name; "Hello." before one is saved |
| Settings | Opens Settings on top |
@@if server
| Ask the server | `POST /v1/hello` with the name; the line under it shows the server's message, or why there was none. One request at a time |
@@end

## Settings

| Element | Does |
| --- | --- |
| Back | Returns to Home without saving. The system's Back does the same |
| Your name | A text field, at most 40 characters |
| Save | Keeps the name on the phone (spaces around it dropped) and returns to Home. The keyboard's action key does the same |

## Not done

- Nothing here follows a design yet. See `design/README.md`.
- Not run on a device.
